  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "uZjHrx8gBCX4BaIE4+nFFJl989M=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:22.468Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "Healthcare is recorded as sufficiently decentralized \u2014 hospitals, Buurtzorg \u2014 with both operational and medium-budget decentralization, standardized on FHIR, and with an established consultancy market naming Better (ex-Marant) and Agitavit. Against that: \"not well connected atm\", and both the PMF question and the companion-software question are marked with a question mark. openEHR is listed as a candidate, with EHRCON26 in Amsterdam on 22\u201323 September as the entry point.\n\nThe mirror-image comparison with construction is instructive. Construction has connections and no consultancy market; healthcare has a consultancy market and no connections. Connections can be built to a schedule \u2014 there is a dated conference in the notes \u2014 whereas a consultancy market cannot be conjured.\n\nOn that reading healthcare is the more tractable of the two gaps, though it needs the companion-software question answered first.",
        "updatedAt": "2026-08-20T10:34:22.468475Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-08-20T10:34:22.468480Z"
    }
  },
